WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.040
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain a teen comedy film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.520
“Wild Child.” Spoilers ahead!&nbsp;
Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.800
The story centers around a spoiled teenage&nbsp;
girl named Poppy Moore living in Malibu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.920
with her widowed father and little sister.&nbsp;
Poppy’s mother died in a car crash long ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.120
and ever since her relationship with her father&nbsp;
Gerry hasn’t been the same. She hates him for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.680
dating women who are not her mother. When his&nbsp;
current girlfriend is about to move in with them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.640
Poppy is furious. She invites her friends&nbsp;
and makes them destroy the woman’s belongings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.000
that are being moved into the house. 
It is not the first time she has pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.040
a prank like this. Gerry is sick and tired of&nbsp;
her making his life more difficult. Till now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.840
he had been excusing her considering that she just&nbsp;
missed her mother but now that Poppy has crossed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.680
a line, he wants to send her to a boarding school&nbsp;
in England. At first, she retaliates but Gerry is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.200
determined to discipline her in the right way. 
At night, Poppy and her little sister Molly talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.640
about her upcoming life in England. Poppy claims&nbsp;
she is relieved people in England at least speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.160
“American”. Molly realizes how out of proportion&nbsp;
her sister is to the real world. She hopes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.760
Poppy will learn something from her stay. The&nbsp;
next day, Poppy’s best friend Ruby helps her pack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.600
and wishes her luck with England’s&nbsp;
weather. She also promises to take care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:32.080
of Poppy’s boyfriend Roddy when she is away. 
In the following scene, Gerry and Poppy arrive at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.640
the boarding school in the countryside in England.&nbsp;
They are welcomed by the school’s headmistress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.800
Mrs. Kingsley who promises to discipline Poppy in&nbsp;
no time. All other students are stunned to see her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.920
in her over-the-top designer outfit. The head&nbsp;
girl of the school, Harriet also lands her eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.520
on her and greets her with a handshake. She is&nbsp;
an egocentric and proud student who thinks she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.720
runs the school. When Poppy refuses to respect&nbsp;
her, she is determined to teach her a lesson. 
&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.320
Poppy finally bids farewell to her&nbsp;
father and walks inside the school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.280
She soon finds out that she has to share a&nbsp;
bedroom with four other girls: Kate, Josie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:13.040
Kiki, and Drippy. She bluntly asks them to get&nbsp;
out because she wants to be left alone but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.760
girls only laugh at her. Then, she is told that&nbsp;
the girls are only allowed to use their phones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.440
on the weekend but Poppy refuses to do so.
A while later, the hostel’s Matron comes to seize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.960
their phones for the week. When Poppy talks to her&nbsp;
sarcastically, she, along with the other girls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:35.040
get detention as punishment. Poppy tries using her&nbsp;
old ways by bribing the Matron but it only gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.480
her in more trouble. On her first day of school,&nbsp;
she modifies the school uniform to fit her taste.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.840
She wears high heels, a tight skirt, and&nbsp;
a cropped blazer, unlike the other girls.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.280
Her roommates warn her that it might get her in&nbsp;
trouble but Poppy, as always, doesn’t care. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.080
she is told about the school’s prefect team&nbsp;
whose leader is the head girl, Harriet. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.680
has a crush on the school’s most popular bachelor&nbsp;
and the headmistress’s son named Freddie. One of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.560
the important rules in the school is that no&nbsp;
girl is allowed to fraternize with any boys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.600
especially Freddie. The headmistress is&nbsp;
strictly against her son dating anyone. 
&nbsp;

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.480
At night before bedtime, the girls ask Poppy&nbsp;
how many guys she has slept with. On hearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.600
the long list, they are shocked because they have&nbsp;
been in the all-girls hostel since they were kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.800
and have no experience with boys whatsoever.&nbsp;
Later, the Matron brings Poppy a proper set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.160
of uniforms to wear from the next day. Poppy&nbsp;
huffs at her and pretends to go to sleep. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:37.040
right after Matron leaves, she goes to the&nbsp;
computer room to email her best friend Ruby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.680
about everything happening in her life. While&nbsp;
she is at it, she notices someone walking outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:47.280
the room. On checking, she finds Drippy in the&nbsp;
freezer having a late-night snack. Just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.800
a fire drill takes place and Poppy is stuck in&nbsp;
the hallways. To not get caught, she climbs on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.400
the roof and enters a bathroom. The bathroom turns&nbsp;
out to be Freddie’s who tells her the way out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.800
promises to keep her visit a secret.
The following day, Poppy is taken into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.840
the school’s lacrosse team. The diva in her is&nbsp;
horrified at girls running around covered in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:13.600
sweat. But when the head girl Harriet challenges&nbsp;
her to a one-on-one match, she accepts it. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.480
launch at each other but instead of hitting the&nbsp;
ball, they start to fistfight. Harriet stops only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.640
when Freddie’s car passes by. She is smitten by&nbsp;
him and hence is horrified when he greets Poppy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:29.920
a good morning. After he drives off, Poppy makes&nbsp;
fun of her for being in love with him. Harriet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.800
runs to her dorm room which consists of several&nbsp;
pictures of Freddie, proving her obsession with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.920
him. She panics about how he knew Poppy’s name but&nbsp;
comes to the conclusion that he was just trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:46.400
hide his love for her by talking to a random girl.&nbsp;
A while later, Poppy is called by the headmistress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:51.440
who is disappointed at her for starting a fight.&nbsp;
She knows that Poppy is not a bad person and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.000
hopes that she will do better in school from&nbsp;
now on. Poppy is amazed by the headmistress’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.280
expectations. For the first time after her&nbsp;
mother’s death, someone has shown faith in her.
&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:06.400
Later that day, Harriet is in her room, when she&nbsp;
notices Poppy sitting right below the window.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.960
She makes her minion dump a bucket of water on&nbsp;
her and pretends like she didn’t know someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:16.720
was downstairs. Poppy has to rush to her room&nbsp;
shivering. She misses her friends from back home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.840
and is feeling homesick. One of her roommates&nbsp;
named Kate notices this and offers Poppy a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.560
jumper for her cold. Poppy feels at home with&nbsp;
Kate and tells her about her mother’s death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:31.200
that happened five years ago. The two talk&nbsp;
about their past and form a bond that Poppy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.600
had never thought she would make with someone&nbsp;
from the school. Kate also gives her a secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:42.720
phone so she can call her friends in America. 
Poppy calls Ruby who turns out to be sleeping with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.960
Poppy’s boyfriend Roddy. They fake being concerned&nbsp;
for her and end the call. Right after, Ruby makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:54.320
fun of Poppy’s appearance and continues making out&nbsp;
with her boyfriend. That night, Poppy’s roommates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:59.360
decide to help her get expelled from school, which&nbsp;
is the only way she can go back to America. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:04.960
she so desperately wants to go home, they feel&nbsp;
sympathetic and want to help. Poppy is overwhelmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.680
by the love they show to her even though she has&nbsp;
been nothing but rude. Starting the next day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:14.880
they play a plethora of pranks; dying the&nbsp;
swimming pool’s water red, prank calling Harriet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:19.920
and spreading rumors about their teachers making&nbsp;
out in the school. For the last one, Poppy gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:25.200
into trouble. She is called to the headmistress’s&nbsp;
office but is let go after a simple warning. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.840
girls register that the headmistress is letting&nbsp;
Poppy off the hook because she is Gerry’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:34.880
daughter. Hence, they will have to do something&nbsp;
out of the ordinary to get her in trouble. 
&nbsp;

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:40.480
When they are in the bath one day, they think of&nbsp;
a brilliant idea. One thing the headmistress hates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:45.600
is her son getting close to any girls from the&nbsp;
school. This means if Poppy made out with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.880
she is bound to be expelled. The next day is&nbsp;
the themed dance party where the people from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.440
the boy’s school will also come. Although&nbsp;
the party is “pride and prejudice” themed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:00.640
Poppy and her group decide to do something extra.&nbsp;
They go to the town to shop for the big day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:06.000
and have a lot of fun. Poppy also changes her hair&nbsp;
color to brunette which makes her look exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.680
like her mother. They secretly steal liquor from&nbsp;
a shop, planning to get wasted at the party.
&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.000
The following evening, everything is going&nbsp;
well. The students are properly dressed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.520
especially Harriet who is dressed as Elizabeth.&nbsp;
She bores Freddie by talking to him in lines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:27.440
from the book. The party is interrupted by Poppy&nbsp;
and her group making a grand entrance in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.640
short modern dresses. Harriet is horrified&nbsp;
but the same cannot be said for Freddie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:37.520
He seems to be attracted to Poppy. The night&nbsp;
turns into a nightmare for the head girl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:42.480
when Freddie and Poppy dance together. She quickly&nbsp;
changes the song to an upbeat one so people would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:49.280
dance individually. Her plan works but then, Poppy&nbsp;
dances alone and steals the show. Later, she and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:56.880
Freddie come outside for some alone time. Harriet&nbsp;
sends her minions to keep an eye on them.
&nbsp;

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:02.880
As the two talk, Poppy realizes Freddie is a quite&nbsp;
interesting man who actually cares about people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:09.040
He leans in to kiss her but the minions interrupt&nbsp;
them. The girls decide not to tell Harriet because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:13.680
she will make their life miserable trying to&nbsp;
separate Freddie and Poppy. Poppy then returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.840
to her friends who are having the time of&nbsp;
their lives with the boys. As they talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:22.160
she confesses that she has never been intimate&nbsp;
with anyone and used to be ashamed about it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:27.360
back home. Hence, she lied to them at first but&nbsp;
now she feels like she can tell them anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:32.000
without the fear of being judged. She also&nbsp;
reveals that she might actually like Freddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.560
not just for the purpose of the prank. 
The next day, Poppy is invited to play lacrosse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.560
after Drippy gets sick. She discovers&nbsp;
her talent for the game and the team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:44.560
wins for the first time because of her.&nbsp;
The next day in the morning assembly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.960
the headmistress announces that their junior&nbsp;
lacrosse team has been selected to play in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:54.160
inter-school competition for the first time in&nbsp;
more than a decade. She asks the participants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:59.040
talk to Harriet if they have any concerns. But&nbsp;
then, she corrects herself because the students&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.840
should now go to Poppy instead of Harriet.
Harriet glows red in anger at the announcement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.040
Starting the next day, Poppy whips the school's&nbsp;
team into shape, getting them into the finals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:15.200
of the competition. Then, one day, she is invited&nbsp;
to a date with Freddie. Before going, she is on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.400
computer sending emails to her friends back home.&nbsp;
She forgets to log it off resulting in someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:25.600
else mishandling her email. Freddie and Poppy&nbsp;
go on a date and talk about different things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.640
They discover they have a lot in common and start&nbsp;
to fall for each other. On returning to her room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:36.000
Poppy finds her friends reading an email&nbsp;
exposing that she thinks of them as losers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.200
The group assumes that the email was sent by&nbsp;
her and is furious. She tries explaining but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.320
girls are so hurt that they refuse to listen. When&nbsp;
Poppy goes to Freddie to talk, she finds out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:51.680
he has also received a similar email, exposing&nbsp;
that she is only using him to get expelled. 
&nbsp;

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:56.080
With no one else to turn to, Poppy sneaks&nbsp;
down to the cook's room and calls Ruby.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.080
She initially pretends to be interested&nbsp;
in what Poppy is talking about but then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:05.360
accidentally reveals how much she dislikes her.&nbsp;
Poppy feels the lowest she has ever been. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:09.920
gets lost in her thoughts and starts playing with&nbsp;
her lighter which accidentally sets a curtain on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:15.760
fire. She immediately puts it out and runs outside&nbsp;
after hearing footsteps approaching. When she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:21.680
back in her room, she looks out her window to see&nbsp;
the fire that she thought was put out has spread.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:27.200
She quickly wakes everyone up but finds out that&nbsp;
Drippy is missing. On realizing that she might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.760
have snuck out for a late-night snack, Poppy&nbsp;
goes to save her. With the firefighter’s help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.680
they manage to get her out safely. 
When the fire is extinguished, Freddie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.800
finds Poppy’s lighter in the mess and assumes&nbsp;
she was the one who lit the fire to get expelled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:46.080
He refuses to hear any explanation and gives&nbsp;
the lighter back to her. Later that day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:51.120
Poppy decides to do the one right thing and&nbsp;
takes the blame for the fire. The headmistress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.680
is disappointed in her but she acknowledges&nbsp;
the fact that Poppy decided to be truthful. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.840
declares that a hearing will be held at the Honor&nbsp;
Court to decide what they should do next. 
&nbsp;

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:06.720
In the following scene, Poppy finds a portrait&nbsp;
of her late mother in the 1976’s lacrosse team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.960
and begins to cry upon realizing her&nbsp;
mother had attended the same school.
&nbsp;

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:15.520
While she waits for the Honor Court hearing,&nbsp;
Freddie finds and is convinced the fire was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:20.800
just an accident. At the same time, Drippy and&nbsp;
the group match the time that the email was sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:25.280
and realize that someone had tried to sabotage&nbsp;
their friendship with Poppy. At the hearing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:30.160
Poppy gives her testimony. Harriet interrupts&nbsp;
her several times and tells her how horrible of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:35.120
a person she is to put everyone’s lives in danger.&nbsp;
When everyone else speaks in Poppy’s favor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:39.520
she panics and accidentally mentions the&nbsp;
lighter. No one had ever said anything about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:44.640
the lighter and no students other than Freddie&nbsp;
knew about it. This proves that Harriet was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:50.160
one who lit the curtains on fire after Poppy&nbsp;
ran away. She confesses that she did it but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:55.600
tries to rationalize it as finishing what Poppy&nbsp;
started. In the end, Poppy is let free without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:00.880
any charges while Harriet is expelled.
In the last scene, Gerry comes to visit his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:06.720
daughter and watches the lacrosse finals game.&nbsp;
Poppy's dramatic change in appearance and attitude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:11.520
surprises him. They win the match, thanks&nbsp;
to her leadership. The father and daughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:15.920
reunite after the game and hug.
